   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " 'Kostya, why did you call?' The second word is a casual way to ask \"why\", more relaxed than the standard word. The action word means \"called\", with the he-word past time frame ending. It's a clumsy question.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "В смысле, я тебе не звонил.",
