  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " 'All right, let us go to the storeroom.' The first phrase translates to \"well, okay\". The next action word carries a casual \"let's go\", literally \"went\". The final phrase is \"to the storeroom\", and the thing word stays in its base form after the connecting word when expressing direction.",
   "gap": 0.4
